Deployment → Endpoint

After model evaluation, the trained model can be deployed as an Endpoint.

=======

1. Server-Based Endpoint

The model runs on a server/instance.
The server is kept running for the endpoint.
Charged based on running time.
You may be charged even when nobody is using the model.

Flow

Trained Model
      ↓
Server-Based Endpoint
      ↓
Server Running
      ↓
Hourly Charges

===

2. Serverless Endpoint
No server needs to be continuously managed by you.
Resources are used when a prediction request comes.
The screenshot describes the charge as prediction-based.
Flow
Trained Model
      ↓
Serverless Endpoint
      ↓
Prediction Request
      ↓
Pay based on usage/predictions

====

| Endpoint                  | Server                        | Charging concept                   |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| **Server-Based Endpoint** | Continuously running          | Charged for running time           |
| **Serverless Endpoint**   | Runs/scales based on requests | Charged based on usage/predictions |

=====

Server-Based = Server running → Time-based cost
Serverless = Prediction request → Usage-based cost

The cost difference follows from how resources are allocated, so 
choosing between server-based and serverless endpoints for different traffic patterns depends mainly on request volume and consistency.

=====

